%% Diagram: Anatomy of an Amazon EventBridge Event
%% Source lecture: AWS EventBridge Crash Course - Lecture: "Event Anatomy & Envelope"
%% Description:  Shows the standard JSON event envelope fields (version, id, source,
%%               detail-type, time, resources, region, account) plus a sample
%%               "Order Placed" custom event payload in the detail field.
%% Author: Prem Vishnoi <prem.vishnoi@example.com>
```mermaid
graph TD
    E[EventBridge Event Envelope<br/>JSON]
    V["version: '0'"]
    ID["id: 'uuid'"]
    SRC["source: 'com.acme.orders'"]
    DT["detail-type: 'Order Placed'"]
    T["time: '2026-10-10T12:00:00Z'"]
    RES["resources: ['order/123']"]
    REG["region: 'us-east-1'"]
    ACC["account: '111122223333'"]
    D["detail: { orderId: 123, amount: 49.99, currency: 'USD' }"]

    E --> V
    E --> ID
    E --> SRC
    E --> DT
    E --> T
    E --> RES
    E --> REG
    E --> ACC
    E --> D
```
